  "pages": "p.2 (connection diagram), p.4-5 (pin descriptions), p.6 (operating ratings: VA/VD 3.0-3.6 V, VDR 2.4 V to VD), p.9 (CLK/PD/OE VIH 2.0 V / VIL 1.0 V), p.10 (tOD 9 ns max parallel mode, tDIS 10 ns typ, latency 7 clocks, 15-65 MHz)",
  "notModeled": [
    "analog inputs and reference (the result is always the 0 V code on both channels)",
    "DF/DCS four-state strap (VA / float = offset binary, AGND / VRM = two's complement, with/without duty-cycle stabilizer): modeled as offset binary (0 V reads 0x800); two's complement is not selectable",
    "MULTIPLEX pin high (both channels multiplexed on DA11-DA0 with ABb on DB0/ABb): only parallel mode (MULTIPLEX low) is modeled",
    "OEB: the clocked bus has one output enable; OEA gates both the A and B data pins in the model, OEB is ignored",
    "VREF reference select levels (analog only)",
    "pipeline latency of 7 clock cycles (the code is constant)",
    "clock frequency limits and power-down exit time; tFloat is the typical tDIS (no maximum given)",
    "vcc is the VDR range (2.4 V to VD 3.6 V); CLK/PD/OE are referenced to VD (3.0-3.6 V)"
  ],
